# CI/CD Delivery Standards

Use these rules when changing CI workflows, deployment setup, or production persistence paths.

1. Keep CI checks in `.github/workflows/ci.yml` aligned with real scripts in `backend/package.json` and `frontend/package.json`.
2. Prefer MVP-fast checks by default; only expand checks when repo baseline issues are resolved.
3. If CI behavior changes, update `docs/DEPLOYMENT_CICD.md` and any related `README.md` setup notes in the same task.
4. Never commit secrets or environment values (`.env`, tokens, API keys) to git.
5. Production storage path changes must remain configurable via env vars (`DATA_DIR`, `UPLOADS_DIR`) and must not break local defaults.
6. Keep deployment docs practical: include one-time setup, verification, and rollback/troubleshooting steps.
